**Architectural Role:** `src/Host/API/Program.cs` is the unified executable entry point for the SCRIPE .NET 10 modular monolith.

- **8-Phase Bootstrap:** Configures Serilog structured telemetry, OpenTelemetry distributed tracing (`AstraFlow.OpenTelemetry`), multi-tenant JWT authentication, 5-Layer PBAC authorization policies, Rate Limiting, CORS, and all **18 Backend Modules**.
- **Server-Role Guards:** Supports running as `All`, `Api`, or `Worker` (background jobs & Outbox processors).

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.Services.AddScripeCore(builder.Configuration);
builder.Services.AddAllScripeModules(builder.Configuration);
```

**Architectural Role:** `src/Core/` defines the universal building blocks inherited by every module.

- **`AuditableEntity`:** Enforces `Guid Id`, `TenantId`, UTC timestamps (`CreatedAt`, `UpdatedAt`), soft-delete (`IsDeleted`), optimistic concurrency (`RowVersion`), and domain event queuing.
- **`Result<T>` Pattern:** Replaces business exceptions across all **596 Commands** and **385 Queries** with explicit `Result.Success(val)` and `Result.Failure<T>(Error)` returns.

```csharp
public abstract class AuditableEntity : BaseEntity, ITenantEntity, ISoftDeletable
{
    public Guid TenantId { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; } = DateTime.UtcNow;
    public bool IsDeleted { get; set; }
}
```

**Architectural Layer:** `Next.js 16 App Router & Route Layouts`

App Router pages, layouts, middleware, route guards, and workspace shell entry points (src/app/).

- **Strict SOLID MVVM Data Flow:** `View (.tsx)` → `ViewModel (use*ViewModel.ts)` → `Repository (*Repository.ts)` → `Service (*Service.ts)` → `IApiService`.
- **Design System & Localization:** 100% `@core/ui/*` primitives, Nexus tokens (`--nx-ground`, `--nx-surface`, `--nx-ink`), and co-located `locales/*.en.ts` + `*.ar.ts` dictionaries.

```tsx
// Strict MVVM View consuming ViewModel & Bilingual Locales
const vm = useFeatureViewModel();
const { t } = useTranslation();
return <Card className="bg-nx-surface border-nx-line">{t("feature.title")}</Card>;
```

